From 89ca6c5484be31f4b8699015e69d4688e4052441 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alimc98 <alimc98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:14:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove a deleted tunnel from the servers it was deployed to
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Deleting a tunnel only dropped the row: the generated config, the core.json
that lists it and the systemd unit all stayed behind, so the tunnel kept
serving users after it vanished from the panel and came back after a reboot.
The configs also accumulate a `.bak.<epoch>` per edit that nothing ever
removes.

Deletion now takes the tunnel off every server it actually ran on: the node
config and its backups go, core.json keeps only the configs still on disk
(so another tunnel sharing the path is restarted into it, not stopped), and
when nothing is left to load the unit is stopped and disabled. A server the
tunnel never reached is left untouched — stopping it would drop whatever it
is serving. Since cleanup disables a unit it empties, deploy enables it again
so a redeployed tunnel survives a reboot.

